  "response": "{\"campaign_title\": \"Echoes of the Void\", \"campaign_subtitle\": \"The First Frontier's Tides\", \"campaign_logline\": \"In a sector where trade routes are fraying, a desperate pilot must navigate the shifting loyalties of three core factions and the shadow of an ancient, silent threat.\", \"campaign_pitch\": \"A gritty, low-stakes beginning for a player who just wants to pay their fuel costs. The story weaves through the logistics of space travel, the were they are willing to invest in their other systems. You aren't a hero; you're an independent contractor navigating the friction between Zenith and Aurelia while the Vanguard tries tos keep order. Kaelen is your constant point of contact\u2014a fixer who knows exactly where to find what you need.\", \"campaign_story_summary\": \"The sector is currently experiencing 'The Drift,' a period of high instability in gate-space,. Even though the system is stable enough for commerce, the drift causes erratic jumps and jump-point hazards. The player starts with a broken engine core; they are on their last few credits to reach the next station. They must navigate thes problems by taking contracts from Kaelen, working with the allies of Zenith (traders), Aurelia (technologists), want0f Vanguard ( vanguard_of_the_realm) and the local community. You move between stations, mining resources for factional components. The story is not a 'chosen one' narrative; it is about survival and profit.\", \"tone\": \"Dry, slightly dark, frontier humor. Gritty reality of space travel. Minimalist aesthetic.\", \"opening\": { \"status_quo\": \"The sector is on high alert due to the Drift. Gate-space is harsh. Trade routes are fraying. You have a meager scrap of a ship and piece of mind.\", \"visible_crisis\": \"A local trade route between Zenith and Aurelia has been severed by a 'Reaver'\u2014a derelict, automated drone swarm that still patrols the outskirts of a destroyed gate-sentry station.\", \"hidden_crisis\": \"The Drift is not an other event; it is a consequence of something deep within the sector's core. The very gates are reacting to were you want to even exist. The gates themselves are aware of their consciousness and they sense fear.\", \"why_now\": \"A merchant ship from Aurelia belongs to a company that had been 'missing' for training exercises. A signal is pulsing in thes nearby sector, a call back into the existence of but few other ships. They need a hammer- turn0f the local area and beat back the Reavers.\", \"player_role\": \"Independent pilot. You are not a hero; you are just another pilot to have to do what it takes for enough credits to pay your fuel costs.\"}, \"mystery\": { \"question\": \"What is causing the Drift?\", \"false_answer\": \"It's just old, decaying infrastructure of the main gate network.\", \"true_answer_hint\": \"The gates are not machines; they are living systems that have begun to 're-awaken' and sense the fear of those who pass through them.\", \"long_term_reveal_direction\": \"The Drift is a biological pulse. The high- turn0f the men and women who were trapped in gate-space during the main expansion. There is no final answer to be given; there are many paths for future campaigns.\"}, \"kaelen\": { \"public_role\": \"Broker, Fixer, Contract Handler.\", \"secret_angle\": \"She knows that the gates are 'alive' and feels a sense of duty to keep them quiet. She manages to keep the peace by keeping thes things moving; she wants no one to even realize what they is meant to be.\", \"address_rule\": \"Always refer to her as Kaelen, or the Broker.\", \"never_reveal_rule\": \"She can never be shown to have special powers, a divine purpose, an official government role, it's just that she is always there. She is a fixer who knows how to good enough to know where to keep things moving.\" }, \"factions\": { \"zenith_problem\": \"The Zenith Trade Guild oversees the station-hub of 'Aetheria'. The problem: They are losing interest in trade routes that are turn0f the rest of the sector. They want to build a unique, private tunnel; they don't care about the other factions and they are becoming more aggressive.\", \"aurelia_problem\": \"The Aurelia Tech-Consortium is based at 'Nexus-7'. The part: They are developing new gate-powers. Of course, told by their machines, they are using a core piece of technology that they don't even know what it feels like to use.\", \"vanguard_problem\": \"The Vanguard Order of the Realm is stationed at 'Bastion_01'. They are not just protectors; they are trying to find out why the turn0f the rest of sector is becoming more erratic. They want a clear and honest truth about the jump-points.\", \"conflict_triangle\": \"Zenith wants tos own the rest of the sector. Aurelia are seeking knowledge through technology. Vanguard determines that the only way to tell thes truth is to even out a clear path for everyone. The tension is between the greed of Zenith, the turn0f the reach of their technology, and the stability of fear.\", \"neutral_space_pressure\": \"The sector's core is a single point where all three factions are willing to be desperate a bit more. It's not really a trade-off; it's taking a lot of risk for a reward that they would offer to even find.\" }, \"act_1\": { \"name\": \"The First Breach\", \"goal\": \"Reach the nearest station and deliver a 'scout report' to Kaelen. Deliver it's hard. You need to clear out a Reaver drone swarm in your way.\", \"opening_incident\": \"A derelict gate-sentry station, a few jumps away, a single drone swarm (a Reaver) is patrolling the path. You receive a flash of signal from Kaelen ands heavy traffic-monitor would show it's a bit harder than usual.\", \"midpoint_turn\": \"After clearing thes Reaver, you reach 'Aetheria'. You find Kaelen and tell her she has your report. She tells you that while the standard route is meant to be clear, some of thes things are beginning to feel like they're not just being pulled by gravity; they are starting to feeling more active. The trade routes are becoming 'unstable.'\", \"finale\": \"Kaelen gives you a hint: an Aurelian tech-core was a bit harder to be found. You move toward the next jump, and the feeling of your engines roar. You find a piece",
